35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, only two firms are bidding for the heavy digging, and both are worried about the clay. It’s going to be tricky.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, that confirms my fear. If the ground is unstable, we can’t just pour concrete. I’m checking how people actually cross the site to see what they need.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, I found the staff numbers are really low, but there are two volunteer groups already helping. Do you think they can manage the daily care?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the basin survived, but the apron failed. I’m checking the planting records to see if the greenery actually held up.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the volunteers are helpful, but the ledger shows planted ground costs triple to maintain. I’m checking if their current commitments can realistically absorb that extra daily workload.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minato, the phasing notes say we can hoard the south, but the centre and gate stay open. That limits where we can dig.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the crossing counts show people stick to firm ground. If the centre stays open, we can’t disrupt that flow.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, if people need firm ground, does that mean we can’t have soft paths? I’m worried about the safety.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the eastern avenue trees died because aftercare was ignored. If we plant again without guaranteed maintenance, we repeat that failure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the ledger confirms the cost gap is widening. I’m checking if the volunteer groups can realistically absorb that extra daily workload.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the centre stays open, we can’t dig there. Does that mean we have to pick a plan that works around the main path?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. The counts show people need firm, open ground. Any plan blocking that flow will fail before the ribbon is cut.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, if the trees died from neglect, does that mean we should avoid planting entirely? I’m worried about the long-term care.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, not avoid it, but guarantee the aftercare. The record shows the trees died because watering was left out of the contract.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the volunteers are committed, but the ledger shows the cost gap is widening. I’m checking if their current commitments can realistically absorb that extra daily workload.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the centre is off-limits, does that force us to the edges? I’m checking if the firms can handle the clay there.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the habitat fund only pays for planting and water, not hard surfaces. So if we avoid the centre, we must design for the edges with green infrastructure.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, if the fund only pays for water and plants, does that mean we can’t build the courts or the market stalls?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the fund terms are strict. It pays for planting and water management only. No surfacing, no buildings. That rules out the market and the courts.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, that confirms my fear. If the fund excludes hard surfaces, we are left with high-maintenance greenery. I am checking if the volunteer groups can realistically absorb that extra daily workload.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
